-- Conformance: a case missing inside a nested constructor pattern is a
-- checker error (Chapter 4, Section 4.9.2).
-- Tests: E311 — exhaustiveness is judged to the full depth of every
-- pattern, so arms that name every constructor at the top and leave a
-- case uncovered inside one are refused, naming it (`Some(Some(_))`).
-- Previously the check read each arm by its outer constructor alone, and
-- a value no arm matches took the last arm (#1540, #1697).
public fn depth(@Option<Option<Int>> -> @Int)
  requires(true)
  ensures(@Int.result >= 0)
  effects(pure)
{
  match @Option<Option<Int>>.0 {
    Some(None) -> 1,
    None -> 0
  }
}
